-- the orbit of an atom under a given list of automorphisms, computed: each automorphism applied to the
-- atom. Every member is in the orbit relation by construction (it carries its witness); the list is the
-- whole orbit exactly when the automorphisms given are all of them, which is a hypothesis about the
-- input and not a property of the computation.
orbit-list : (M : Mol) → List (Auto M) → mol-atoms M → List (mol-atoms M)
orbit-list M autos x = map (λ a → auto-fun M a x) autos
